source: ASF Jira Server 8.20.10, POST /rest/api/1.0/render (hack/jira-render-evidence.py), captured 2026-08-23
observed: Jira consumes the backslash before `?` and shows the bare character, so `?` is escapable and the Jira parser decodes it.
-- input.jira --
a\?
-- rendered.html --
<p>a&#63;</p>
-- want.md --
a?
